From: Rosen Penev <rosenp@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ibm: emac: convert to phylink

Replace the driver's own PHY layer (phy.c, link polling work and the
mii_phy wrappers around phylib) with phylink.

phylink now handles PHYs from "phy-handle", "fixed-link" and the link
state reporting, ethtool link settings, pause settings and MII ioctls.
The MAC is reprogrammed from mac_link_up()/mac_link_down() the same way
the link timer did before.

Device trees with neither a PHY nor a fixed-link ("phy-map" and
"phy-address" absent) keep the old 100 Mbps full duplex link through
phylink_set_fixed_link(). Device trees that only describe the PHY with
"phy-map"/"phy-address" get an MDIO bus whose phy_mask comes from these
properties, and the first PHY found is connected to phylink. The PHYs
then use their phylib drivers instead of the init sequences in phy.c.

The GPCS reset needed for SGMII/TBI/RTBI stays in emac_configure().

Signed-off-by: Rosen Penev <rosenp@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: LLM
